  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 128 AM CDT Thu Apr 23 2026\n\nThe upcoming weekend calls for dry and warmer weather across South \nCentral Texas for the most part. When it comes to the afternoon into \nthe evening hours, the cap could hold and nothing happen or could \nerode enough for storms to develop quickly. With that said, favoring \nthe dry conditions through the period. The one thing we have medium \nto high confidence is about the heat that arrives over the weekend. \nForecast highs for Saturday and Sunday in the 90s with heat index \nvalues near 100 along the I-35 Corridor and the Coastal Plains and \nexceeding the 100 mark over the southern part of the Rio Grande. So, \nthe forecast message is that hot conditions are likely and we all \nneed to make sure to stay hydrated and take breaks if working or \ndoing any sports or activities outside.\n\nThe heat continues into early next week. Rain chances could return \non Monday as a frontal boundary pushes across the local area, \nbut models are not in agreement yet.",
